From: pgf@srl02.cacs.usl.edu (Phil G. Fraering)
Date: Wed, 21 Sep 1994 17:39:52 -0500
Subject: [#94-9-351] SCI: role for Q.M in neurobiology

About the possible advantages in Penrose's constructs over something
that operates like a standard neural network, please consider this: a
trait only needs to confer a 5% survival advantage in order to become
ubiquitous in a population over a reasonably short time (a couple
hundred generations); if this were the case for that trait, or even if
it conferred something like a .01% survival advantage, over a large
enough time period, and 4 billion years would be enough, especially
for fast-breeding lower life forms, it only needs to happen once in
our "chain of descent."

Phil

