Date: Wed, 21 Sep 1994 17:42:58 -0500
Subject: [#94-9-352] Quantum Erasers (fwd)

Before we get too tied up in theoretical physics, let
me postulate the following for fun:

There is no Grand Unified Theory. The Universe as a whole
does not make sense in terms of a single mathematical model.

Now a question I'd like to ask is, is this more or less rational,
or more or less "mystical," than the standard model in which every-
thing is assumed to interrelate in some fashion or another?

Phil


